    "title": "Trump Vetoes Drinking Water Bill in Colorado, Prompting Criticism from Representative Boebert",
    "text": "• Donald Trump vetoed a bill that would have funded a drinking water project in Lauren Boebert's Colorado district.\n• The bill aimed to provide safe drinking water to 39 communities in Colorado's eastern plains.\n• Trump stated in his veto letter that his administration is committed to preventing American taxpayers from funding expensive and unreliable policies.\n• Boebert criticized the veto, calling the bill \"completely non-controversial.\"\n• Boebert suggested the veto might be political retaliation for her pushing the administration to release files on Jeffrey Epstein.\n• Trump also vetoed a bill for a project in Florida to protect an area within Everglades National Park inhabited by the Miccosukee Tribe.\n• Trump stated the tribe was never authorized to inhabit the Osceola Camp area.\n• Trump's vetoes were the first two of his second term.\n• The veto of the Colorado bill came after Trump's vow to retaliate against Colorado for keeping Tina Peters in prison.\n• Tina Peters is a former Colorado county clerk serving a nine-year prison term for illegally tampering with voting machines.\n• Boebert stated that the veto denies clean drinking water to 50,000 people in Southeast Colorado.",
